<statement>
<p>It is estimated that 41<percent/> of Kickstarter projects are successfully funded. Assume each Kickstarter project is independent. A random sample of 15 Kickstarter projects are followed. Let <m>\displaystyle{X}</m> be the number Kickstarter projects that are successfully funded. Calculate the following:</p>
<p>a. <m>\displaystyle\mu_{{X}}</m>: <fillin characters="4" /></p>
<p>b. <m>\displaystyle\sigma_{{X}}</m>: <fillin characters="4" /></p>
<p>c. <m>\displaystyle{P}{\left({X}={6}\right)}</m>: <fillin characters="4" /></p>
<p>d. <m>\displaystyle{P}{\left({X}{<}{8}\right)}</m>: <fillin characters="4" /></p>
<p>e. <m>\displaystyle{P}{\left({X}{>}{4}\right)}</m>: <fillin characters="4" /></p>
<p>f.  <m>\displaystyle{P}{\left({X}\geq{4}\right)}</m>: <fillin characters="4" /></p>
<p>g. <m>\displaystyle{P}{\left({5}\leq{X}\leq{8}\right)}</m>: <fillin characters="20" /></p>

</statement>
<answer>
<p><ul><li>6.15</li><li>1.9048621997404</li><li>0.20595641655568</li><li>0.76260921895035</li><li>0.8051873106088</li><li>0.92150351081973</li><li>0.69567089314146</li></ul></p>
</answer>

